WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.882
Hi! In situational writing, you get a situation and write an email, a letter or a note. The secret is three letters: P, A and C. Let's learn them.

2
00:00:13.032 --> 00:00:20.442
P is purpose: why are you writing? To invite, to apologise, to inform, or to ask for something?

3
00:00:20.592 --> 00:00:28.026
A is audience: who will read it? A friend, a teacher or the principal? This decides your tone.

4
00:00:28.176 --> 00:00:35.010
C is context: what happened? Make the time, place and reason clear.

5
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:44.130
To a friend, you can be informal: Hi Jo. To a teacher, be formal: Dear, then Mr or Mrs and the teacher's surname.

6
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:51.018
To a friend you might say: Guess what! To a teacher: I am writing to inform you that...

7
00:00:51.168 --> 00:00:59.202
Closings are different too: Cheers or See you for a friend, Yours sincerely or Thank you for a teacher.

8
00:00:59.352 --> 00:01:07.290
The task lists several points, such as the time, place, reason and request. Include every one, or you'll lose marks.

9
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:14.082
Join the points into smooth sentences in your own words. Don't copy the task word for word.

10
00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:19.098
When you finish, tick off each point one by one.

11
00:01:19.248 --> 00:01:26.490
Watch out! Starting an email to the principal with Hey! What's up? is far too casual!

12
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:33.762
The reader is the principal, so use a formal greeting and tone, like Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to...

13
00:01:33.912 --> 00:01:39.162
So before you start, think about A: who is reading?

14
00:01:39.312 --> 00:01:51.522
Your turn! You're emailing a good friend to invite them to your birthday party. Should the tone be formal or informal? Pause and think.

15
00:01:51.672 --> 00:01:59.418
The answer is informal. You can start with Hi and end with See you there. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:59.568 --> 00:02:12.594
Another one! The points are the date, time, place and what to bring. You've only written the date and place. What's missing? Pause and think.

17
00:02:12.744 --> 00:02:20.370
You've missed the time and what to bring. Every point must be included. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:32.322
Here's another! You're writing to your form teacher to explain why you were absent. Which opening is better? Pause and think.

19
00:02:32.472 --> 00:02:40.842
The answer is B. It uses a formal greeting and states the purpose straight away. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:40.992 --> 00:02:51.426
One more! In an email to the principal, should you close with Cheers or Yours sincerely? Pause and think.

21
00:02:51.576 --> 00:02:58.890
The answer is Yours sincerely. It's formal and polite. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:10.818
Remember: before writing, think PAC: why you're writing, who will read it, and what happened. Include every point, match the tone to the reader, and tick off each point at the end.

23
00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:15.786
Try writing a short note to someone in your family!

